-- title:
--   Galois conjugation of period-p expansions via a diamond operator
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $M \neq 0$ and $p$ with $p$ prime and $p \nmid M$, and a natural number $m$. Let $G \colon \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be holomorphic (differentiable as a map of complex manifolds), invariant in the sense that $G(g \cdot \tau) = G(\tau)$ for every $g \in \Gamma_1(Mp)$ and every $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$, such that for every $\alpha \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the product $(\tau \mapsto G(\alpha \cdot \tau)) \cdot \Delta^m$ is bounded at $i\infty$, and such that every coefficient of the period-$1$ $q$-expansion of $G \cdot \Delta^m$ is rational. Let $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ have lower-right entry $\gamma_{1,1}$ divisible by $p$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by $\zeta = e^{2\pi i/p}$, let $b$ be coprime to $p$, and let $\varphi \colon K \to \mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism sending any element of $K$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ is $\zeta$ to $\zeta^{b}$. Let $\delta \in \Gamma_0(Mp)$ have upper-left entry congruent to $b$ modulo $p$ and to $1$ modulo $M$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Then there is an element $z \in K$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ is the $n$-th coefficient of the period-$p$ $q$-expansion of $(\tau \mapsto G(\gamma \cdot \tau)) \cdot \Delta^m$, and the $n$-th coefficient of the period-$p$ $q$-expansion of $(\tau \mapsto G((\delta\gamma) \cdot \tau)) \cdot \Delta^m$ equals $\varphi(z)$.
--
--   This is the form taken here by Shimura's reciprocity law at the cusps: coefficientwise application of the automorphism $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{b}$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ to the period-$p$ Fourier expansion of a $\Gamma_1(Mp)$-invariant function at the cusp $\gamma\infty$ produces the expansion at $\delta\gamma\infty$, that is, the effect of a diamond operator. It is used in the corresponding statement for Atkin–Lehner slashes, [`ModularCurve.exists_qExpansion_coeff_atkinLehnerSlash_eq_and_slash_mul_eq_apply_gamma1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_qExpansion_coeff_atkinLehnerSlash_eq_and_slash_mul_eq_apply_gamma1_mul), and rests on the general version [`ModularCurve.exists_qExpansion_comp_smul_coeff_eq_and_eq_apply_of_gamma_invariant`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_qExpansion_comp_smul_coeff_eq_and_eq_apply_of_gamma_invariant) together with [`ModularCurve.qExpansion_coeff_comp_smul_mem_adjoin_exp_of_gamma1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.qExpansion_coeff_comp_smul_mem_adjoin_exp_of_gamma1_mul).
